PART II: END USER LICENSE AGREEMENT (EULA)

2. Grant of Personal & Non-Commercial License
   Subject to strict, continuous compliance with every clause of this Agreement,
   the Licensor grants to individual human End Users ("Users") a personal,
   worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to download, install, execute,
   and inspect the System solely for lawful, human-crafted, non-commercial,
   educational, or authorized sovereign public-infrastructure purposes.

3. Principle 1 — Perpetual Usability & Anti-Obsolescence ("Stop Killing Anything")
   3.1 Right to Continued Operation: Once any game, application, engine tool,
       or digital work is distributed or executed on this System, the End User
       retains an irrevocable, perpetual right to run, archive, and preserve
       that work locally or on private community servers forever.
   3.2 Ban on Remote Kill-Switches: No developer, publisher, or vendor may embed
       remote termination triggers, expiration timers, or mandatory central
       server dependencies designed to disable or degrade software after
       release. Before shutting down any official online service, the creator
       must release standalone server binaries and full offline support.

4. Principle 2 — Absolute Prohibition of DRM
   4.1 Zero-DRM Environment: Digital Rights Management (DRM), always-online
       authentication checks, hardware-tethering locks, kernel-level anti-cheat
       rootkits, and encrypted license wrappers are strictly forbidden.
   4.2 Nullification of Restrictive Wrappers: Any attempt to wrap System files
       or System-hosted software inside proprietary DRM is void from inception
       and constitutes an immediate breach of this EULA.

5. Principle 3 — Prohibition of Generative AI Game Development & "Slop" Content
   5.1 Ban on AI-Generated Games & Slop: Using generative AI or automated
       content pipelines to build games, generate code, synthesize art/audio,
       or flood the ecosystem with mass-produced, low-effort, or derivative
       "slop" content on or through this System is strictly prohibited and
       deemed an unauthorized, unlawful exploitation of the Licensor's framework.
   5.2 Human Craftsmanship Requirement: Software and games created for this
       System must represent genuine human authorship and engineering rather
       than automated AI slop generation.
   5.3 No Circumvention via Rebranding or Alternate AI Forms: Users and entities
       may not bypass Section 5.1 by calling an AI system by another name
       (including but not limited to "autonomous agents," "assisted synthesis,"
       "procedural neural tools," "synthetic datasets," or any newly invented
       industry jargon). Any automated system functioning as generative AI or
       producing AI slop is strictly covered and barred.

