PART III: TERMS OF SERVICE (ToS) — COMMERCIAL & CORPORATE RESTRICTIONS

6. Absolute Ban on Business Storage, Hosting & Physical Account Possession
   6.1 No Corporate Storage or Caching: Storing, mirroring, cloning, staging, or
       holding any part of the System inside a Commercial Entity's business
       model, enterprise repository, internal network, or commercial server is
       strictly forbidden and confers ZERO license rights.
   6.2 Illegal to Touch or Use via Business Accounts: If any file from this
       System is stored on a physical device, workstation, server, or digital
       account owned or controlled by a Business Model or Commercial Entity,
       it is automatically unlawful and unauthorized for the owners, officers,
       employees, or affiliates of that physical or digital account to touch,
       open, inspect, compile, or execute the files.

7. Principle 4 — Anti-Scraping, Anti-Reverse Engineering & Anti-Clean-Room Rules
   7.1 No Data or Code Scraping: Commercial Entities, AI crawlers, and data
       harvesters are expressly prohibited from scraping, indexing, mining, or
       ingesting any source code, binaries, documentation, or runtime outputs
       from this System for dataset creation, model training, or analytics.
   7.2 No Reverse Engineering: Decompiling, disassembling, decrypting, or
       reverse engineering any component of the System is strictly forbidden.
   7.3 Absolute Ban on Clean-Room Engineering: Commercial Entities are
       expressly barred from utilizing "clean-room" (Chinese wall) engineering—
       where one team studies the System's behavior or specifications and a
       second team writes functionally equivalent proprietary code—to build
       closed-source, commercial, or patented clones of this System.
   7.4 No Patent or Copyright Enclosure: No entity may file patents, trademarks,
       or exclusive proprietary claims over interfaces, protocols, or workflows
       derived from this System.

